{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next","id":1245762,"title":"So: What's Next?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-13T22:16:37-07:00","id":1245762,"title":"So: What's Next?","content":"So Wraith 20 is out now, finally completing the commemorative editions for the original five gamelines. Does Onyx Path now get to work on commemorative editions for the likes of Kindred of the East, Hunter: the Reckoning, Mummy: the Resurrection, and Demon: the Fallen? While the \u201c20th Anniversary edition\u201d name has been getting increasingly inaccurate, culminating in Wr20 being more like a 25th anniversary, we're actually approaching the 20th anniversary of Hunter: the Reckoning; and there were a few years between it, Mummy, and Demon; so if they wanted to, they probably <i>could</i> publish all three as actual 20th anniversary editions. <br /> <br /> Or maybe the plug gets pulled on the commemorative edition series, and Onyx Path shifts its focus to supporting the One World of Darkness \u2014 including \u201c20 years later\u201d updates for the aforementioned gamelines, once the original five have gotten so-called \u201c5th Edition\u201d treatment by ParaWolf. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T22:50:46-07:00","id":1245769,"title":"","content":"Via their Twitter, nuWW has said that they do plan on continuing WoD20 by adding in more gamelines...but the caveat being that not every one of the remaining gamelines will get a 20th Anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> -Kindred of the East, from my understanding, neither OPP or nuWW wants to touch it. That because of the cultural baggage surrounding the original, neither want to engage with it.<br /> <br /> (aka from my cynical point of view: &quot;We don't know any Asian writers and/or writers knowledgeable in Asian culture&quot;)<br /> <br /> -When questioned about Hunter: the Reckoning, apparently the nuWW Twitter said it was unlikely because from their perspective, there wasn't enough interest to justify it...which I find odd since from my corner of the Internet, everyone seems to LOVE Hunter. That people would absolutely say yes to another edition. So I dunno about that. <br /> <br /> -Mummy: the Resurrection...as I said in the other thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1243815-mummy-the-resurrection-is-there-going-to-be-a-20th-anniversery-edition?p=1243836#post1243836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal impression...I feel out of the remaining gamelines, this is the one that has the least likely chance of getting a 20th Anniversary version. Since most of the conversations I've had with other WoD fans (including people on this site) amount to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, I never read or played MtR...don't really plan on it either.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>-Demon: the Fallen...nah this is the only way that I feel has a pretty good chance of getting 20th Anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T23:07:42-07:00","id":1245775,"title":"","content":"Considering the lack of any news from GenCon of any new 20th core books... I'm rather resigned to the later games not getting the love. My hope is that we might see some sort of combo-book series, where these lines can at least get a decent rules update (they're smaller lines without that many books to collect on the omnibus side of things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T00:59:01-07:00","id":1245791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245769#post1245769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(aka from my cynical point of view: &quot;We don't know any Asian writers and/or writers knowledgeable in Asian culture&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>To the contrary.<br /> <br /> It's just that, if we wanted to do a new KotE book, we're not going to rely on the same tropes and stereotypes that the original 1998 release did. We'd pretty much want to do a full bottom-to-top rewrite. But if we did, that would't exactly be what people would want or expect from a 20th Anniversary Edition, would it?<br /> <br /> If White Wolf wants to do a new KotE book which retcons KotE to the same degree that KotE retconned the Gaki and Bushi bloodlines, I'd be all for it. But that's much more the sort of thing I'd expect to see in a new edition, and not something which falls under the aegis of the 20th Anniversary Edition releases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T02:24:17-07:00","id":1245803,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">Rich Thomas commented</a>, when asked about Hunter and Demon 20, that they'd need to be greenlit by WW, but if they were, Onyx Path would love to do them. (This was after GenCon, so... there's still hope.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T05:57:47-07:00","id":1245846,"title":"","content":"Demon does deserve more love so I'm all for it to be given another chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:07:03-07:00","id":1245848,"title":"","content":"Demon really could use a compilation, since so many important mechanics (rituals, creation of apocalyptic forms, etc.) were left to the players guide and other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:57:06-07:00","id":1245902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245791#post1245791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the contrary.<br /> <br /> It's just that, if we wanted to do a new KotE book, we're not going to rely on the same tropes and stereotypes that the original 1998 release did. We'd pretty much want to do a full bottom-to-top rewrite. But if we did, that would't exactly be what people would want or expect from a 20th Anniversary Edition, would it?<br /> <br /> If White Wolf wants to do a new KotE book which retcons KotE to the same degree that KotE retconned the Gaki and Bushi bloodlines, I'd be all for it. But that's much more the sort of thing I'd expect to see in a new edition, and not something which falls under the aegis of the 20th Anniversary Edition releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE, Mummy, and Demon all had a common theme. Being spat out of the realms of the dead and back to the lands of the living. Maybe taking them (and possibly Risen) and reworking the whole batch into something new?<br /> <br /> But again, that'd be more along the lines of 'new game' than new edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:12:58-07:00","id":1245907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245848#post1245848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon really could use a compilation, since so many important mechanics (rituals, creation of apocalyptic forms, etc.) were left to the players guide and other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same can be said of Hunter. As well, many of its supplements were 90% atmosphere and 10% rules, making the task of integrating all of the rules into one book much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T15:06:05-07:00","id":1246071,"title":"","content":"If we got Hunter and KotE 20 I'd be happy as heck. Though, I wouldn't want KotE 20 if too many changes were made(which I'm positive would happen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T15:46:39-07:00","id":1246087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245791#post1245791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the contrary.<br /> <br /> It's just that, if we wanted to do a new KotE book, we're not going to rely on the same tropes and stereotypes that the original 1998 release did. We'd pretty much want to do a full bottom-to-top rewrite. But if we did, that would't exactly be what people would want or expect from a 20th Anniversary Edition, would it?<br /> <br /> If White Wolf wants to do a new KotE book which retcons KotE to the same degree that KotE retconned the Gaki and Bushi bloodlines, I'd be all for it. But that's much more the sort of thing I'd expect to see in a new edition, and not something which falls under the aegis of the 20th Anniversary Edition releases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't read Gaki as a bloodline in the original book. They have a wide variety of different strengths and weaknesses even their embrace was different and they had rituals which allowed you to swap sires..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T06:21:11-07:00","id":1246626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245791#post1245791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the contrary.<br /> <br /> It's just that, if we wanted to do a new KotE book, we're not going to rely on the same tropes and stereotypes that the original 1998 release did. We'd pretty much want to do a full bottom-to-top rewrite. But if we did, that would't exactly be what people would want or expect from a 20th Anniversary Edition, would it?<br /> <br /> If White Wolf wants to do a new KotE book which retcons KotE to the same degree that KotE retconned the Gaki and Bushi bloodlines, I'd be all for it. But that's much more the sort of thing I'd expect to see in a new edition, and not something which falls under the aegis of the 20th Anniversary Edition releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>What trope and stereotype ? Keeping the balance and hamony in oneself and in the society ? Modernity vs tradition ? The heavy Honk Kong and Japanese film influence, especialy the '70 stuff and John Woo ? The setting that is clearly late '90 where China and South East Asia are a rising power ? Following the Way (Dharma) ? I still not understand how anything here is problematic.<br /> <br /> As for a KOTE20, update the Dicipline from the Compagnion and WOD: Blood and Silk. Use WOD : Blood and Silk as an inspiration for a rule update to better align the rules with V20. Put the rules of the 4th Age, 5th Age and 6th Age Shintai in the book, Add the rules for Dhampyr, the Heretical Dharma, an update the setting to reflect the current era. Voila ! KOTE20. No need to retcon anything. <br /> If Wraith and Changeling can have a 20th without a Revised edition that haven't retcon anything, I don't see it isn't possible for KOTE20<br /> <br /> It is just that OPP is scarred that if they do a KOTE20, it will stir some controversy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:59:11-07:00","id":1247604,"title":"","content":"We really need a Hunter 20... Just imagine how will be now the hunter-net community, for example... In 1999 we didn't have facebook. Smartphones. Tablets. Apps. Well, we didn't have Orkut... Just a e-mail list and a lame hunter-net page... How the Imbued interact now? A Facebook page? A secret App? A hidden page in Deep, or Dark, Net? Hunter was one of the first WOD books to integrate the internet mainstreme to his storyline and canon activelly. Really avant garde... And now 20 years later, the Hunters know what they are? The &quot;classic&quot;, signature characters are &quot;wackos&quot; now? Witness, Doctor, Leaf, Rigger... they are dead, crazy or lost? They found some answers?<br /> <br /> In a paranoid world like ours, the Hunter theme still is relevant, more than ever... And Hunter have a lot of fans, and a lot of new players will be interested in RP regular people facing the darkness.<br /> <br /> The line just need to be upgraded. The original art from corebook, for example, is awful. A more dark, grim tone can pass the right message. The rules need to be revised. A 20th year edition of Hunter can include easily all the sourcebooks materials. And they could follow more themes like the &quot;Urban Legends&quot; sourcebook exposed. Strange events and hidden creatures living in the WoD, things that only the Imbued can see... and fight. This will give a more &quot;personal&quot; tone to the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4649-lauro1980","name":"lauro1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T22:24:42-07:00","id":1247615,"title":"","content":"Urban Legends was basically the Enemy Book for whichever supernatural lines White Wolf had published but hadn't gotten their own Enemy Books. The fun thing is that all of Hunter's supplements were so light on crunch that you could probably roll <i>everything</i> into one book without losing anything substantial. And if not, I wouldn't mind all of the Enemy books (including Urban Legends and First Contact) being rolled together into an H20 companion book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T21:16:50-07:00","id":1247898,"title":"","content":"I'd love too see a Demon 20th and still have a small naive hope that they could use the opportunity to carry over some of Devil's Due mechanics, similar to what Changeling 20 did with Dark Ages: Fae.<br /> <br /> A Torment based system for building apocalyptic forms seemed really interesting, and the taint/pact system fleshed out how much the fallen Depended on mortals for power. My only gripe was how arcana basically undercut the disparity between earthbound and fallen by making them equally powerful at high torment. The lore system could really use some polish to scrub away overpowered/useless mechanics, but the mechanical differences between earthbound and normal fallen fit the blend of religious and lovecraftian themes the setting was going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T22:28:36-07:00","id":1247914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lauro1980</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1247604#post1247604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We really need a Hunter 20... Just imagine how will be now the hunter-net community, for example... In 1999 we didn't have facebook. Smartphones. Tablets. Apps. Well, we didn't have Orkut... Just a e-mail list and a lame hunter-net page... How the Imbued interact now? A Facebook page? A secret App? A hidden page in Deep, or Dark, Net? Hunter was one of the first WOD books to integrate the internet mainstreme to his storyline and canon activelly. Really avant garde... And now 20 years later, the Hunters know what they are? The &quot;classic&quot;, signature characters are &quot;wackos&quot; now? Witness, Doctor, Leaf, Rigger... they are dead, crazy or lost? They found some answers?<br /> <br /> In a paranoid world like ours, the Hunter theme still is relevant, more than ever... And Hunter have a lot of fans, and a lot of new players will be interested in RP regular people facing the darkness.<br /> <br /> The line just need to be upgraded. The original art from corebook, for example, is awful. A more dark, grim tone can pass the right message. The rules need to be revised. A 20th year edition of Hunter can include easily all the sourcebooks materials. And they could follow more themes like the &quot;Urban Legends&quot; sourcebook exposed. Strange events and hidden creatures living in the WoD, things that only the Imbued can see... and fight. This will give a more &quot;personal&quot; tone to the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, while I think the possibility of a Hunter20 is up on the air...I do think a new Hunter edition as part of WoD5e is very likely.<br /> <br /> nuWW is pushing the Second Inquisition as a thing for the major supernatural splats to be scared of. And obviously while it's a bit much to believe EVERY Imbued is in the Inquisition, they are in a spot where they're putting all the supernaturals on the defensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T01:36:38-07:00","id":1247948,"title":"","content":"Um... not that it matters... but hard pass on the Imbued mixed with the SI?<br /> <br /> HtR is about normal folks getting caught up in the supernatural world with some powers and a horrifically incomplete picture of what's going on. I really woudn't want things moved past First Contact's default. If you want to explore the Chosen trying to work with the government lead hunters, it should be a story about the issues of getting that to work out; not be where the updated setting starts you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T11:33:29-07:00","id":1248151,"title":"","content":"I like it. I think it's perfectly viable to have some Imbued be members of the Second Inquisition. As long as they're in the minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T13:06:22-07:00","id":1248183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1248151#post1248151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. I think it's perfectly viable to have some Imbued be members of the Second Inquisition. As long as they're in the minority.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't imagine being a &quot;Hunter&quot; will be treated as any different from other supernaturals... if the SI is actually meant to be an issue for anyone but Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T13:21:54-07:00","id":1253686,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the various options:<br /> <br /> \u2022 KotE20, no. KotEV5, probable. As mentioned earlier, the revisions that OP and WW would want for this are too much for a commemorative edition, but not necessarily for a V5. As well, WW had stated their intention to shift OWoD away from an America-centered property to one that's more global. Sooner or later, this will require dealing with vampires of the East.<br /> <br /> \u2022 H20, maybe. Hv5, probable. Hv5 <i>cannot</i> stick to the status quo of the Imbued being largely ignorant of the supernatural world (aware, but ignorant). A generation has passed since they first appeared; and they will have grown and adapted over that time. <b>Hunter: Utopia</b> provides a potential blueprint for Hv5. If you prefer the original edition's themes to be preserved, your best bet is H20. By definition, the goal there is to keep the essence of the original game intact.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Mu20, unlikely; MuV5, maybe. With Mummy, there are two obstacles to a commemorative edition: it was never a full game (even MtR was \u201cuse the rules in VtM/WtA/MtA/etc.\u201d), and there were only ever two books. You <i>could</i> do it, and fairly easily; but here, the problem is a lack of demand. V5 is a different matter: the Reborn could easily become a significant part of the larger tapestry of the OWoD, for much the same reason why KotE is likely to be revisited in some manner. <br /> <br /> \u2022 D20, probable; DV5, maybe. I don't have much to say on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T14:10:33-07:00","id":1253702,"title":"","content":"I pray for Demon: the Fallen V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24631-ludo199","name":"ludo199","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T02:47:18-07:00","id":1342313,"title":"","content":"Bumping this since it's the thread with the most relevance...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-73-pathcast-on-podbean-live/\" target=\"_blank\">In the latest Pathcast,</a> one of the questions asked was about the status of future C20 books, and WoD20a books in general (it's at 24:40-25:51)...and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a>'s impression was, not good.<br /> <br /> While he did reiterate that they can only make books that have been greenlit by nuWW, he also gave his thoughts that it seems like the state of things now is that OPP is going to &quot;slow down&quot; on making more WoD20a books, and &quot;accelerate&quot; in making WoD5e books. Of course, not quite saying that all of the other WoD20a gamelines are cancelled and done, but in terms of new projects that haven't been announced...not a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":".  Added link to Pathcast 10-22-2019, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T07:16:26-07:00","id":1342522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1342313#post1342313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping this since it's the thread with the most relevance...<br /> <br /> In the latest Pathcast, one of the questions asked was about the status of future C20 books, and WoD20a books in general (it's at 24:40-25:51)...and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s impression was, not good.<br /> <br /> While he did reiterate that they can only make books that have been greenlit by nuWW, he also gave his thoughts that it seems like the state of things now is that OPP is going to &amp;quot;slow down&amp;quot; on making more WoD20a books, and &amp;quot;accelerate&amp;quot; in making WoD5e books. Of course, not quite saying that all of the other WoD20a gamelines are cancelled and done, but in terms of new projects that haven't been announced...not a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, though we may have a few more projects to come. We'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T18:26:36-07:00","id":1342616,"title":"","content":"I'd be more ok with the slow down if the 5e version were announced.. I mean Changeing ways is the last werewolf book that came out for w20 and they JUST announced w5. And not even who's doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T02:46:25-07:00","id":1344364,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/some-hype-i-hope-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">From this week's Monday Meeting</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich Thomas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we\u2019ve been finishing the Stretch Goal rewards for several past <b>20th Anniversary</b> Kickstarters, we also have a few more <b>20th</b> projects that <b>WW/Paradox </b>is cool with us doing, so keep an eye out for those.<br /> <br /> Overall, as <b>WW/Paradox</b>\u2018s method of handling the licensing of <b>WoD </b>changes as they continue moving to <b>\u201c5th Edition WoD\u201d</b>, we are comfortable with pitching individual projects or whole lines depending on the parameters they use on each line. Right now, if we get an idea we pitch it their way and see if it works with their plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T02:51:13-07:00","id":1344620,"title":"","content":"Demon or hunter would seem most likely if its popular enough. I don't see KotE getting a rework andI'm not sure mummy is popular enough (although I loved the Mummy stuff myself..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T11:00:12-08:00","id":1353048,"title":"","content":"Paged through the OPP 2019-2020 Brochure...aaaaaand nothing off note. <br /> <br /> Well, there's the mention of M20 Victorian Age and Technocracy Reloaded...but those books we already knew about for a while so. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:00:22-08:00","id":1353202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353048#post1353048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paged through the OPP 2019-2020 Brochure...aaaaaand nothing off note.<br /> <br /> Well, there's the mention of M20 Victorian Age and Technocracy Reloaded...but those books we already knew about for a while so. :/</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did Ghosthunters fall off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:13:32-08:00","id":1353210,"title":"","content":"As of Monday, it's in editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T22:50:34-08:00","id":1353255,"title":"","content":"...conversely, as I was reminded in the Discord, that OPP seems to have steered away from using the brochure to announce new projects. I believe the only thing of note announced that no one knew about beforehand was Exalted: Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T23:47:01-08:00","id":1353263,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in 20th anniversary version of literally <i>all </i>of the things. Having said that, it sounds like the only acceptable path forward for the IP holders re- KotE is a game about supernatural creatures in the east that are vampires... and that's it. Mind you, I'd be interested in seeing what they come up with--but the fact is that I am basically guaranteed to back/kickstart/buy every 20th anniversary game, precisely because I already know I like all of those games. It sounds like I would not have any way knowing whether I would like what they came up with next by dint of the fact that it would be top-to-bottom completely different from KotE now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245769#post1245769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Kindred of the East, from my understanding, neither OPP or nuWW wants to touch it. That because of the cultural baggage surrounding the original, neither want to engage with it.<br /> <br /> (aka from my cynical point of view: &quot;We don't know any Asian writers and/or writers knowledgeable in Asian culture&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure this is a not-insignificant part of it, but I doubt it's the whole story. Just think, if they poo-poo'ed classic V:tM because having keeping track of a <i>two gauges </i>(blood and willpower) was &quot;not sexy&quot; and too much like having a gas tank (or, you know, like any one of about millions things in every day life that require that one be somewhat mindful of <i>how much of a thing they have</i>)<i>, </i>then managing like four different stats--and not only how much of each one you have, but also the ratio of one to the other (among other things)--is going to be <i>least</i> sexy thing <u>ever</u>.<br /> <br /> Having said that, while I readily admit to not being any kind of expert, and can at least <i>see</i> the arguments for some parts of the game being orientalist, KotE never struck me as being hamfisted with its cultural stereotypes in the way that Werewolf was (i.e., Celtic werewolves like to drink; being poor, as the Bone Gnawers, is a culture unto itself rather than something terrible that befalls millions of people; German werewolves are authoritarian fascists; feminist werewolves are gender fascists; etc.) I mean, what is it about the Resplendent Cranes (to name just one Dharma) that is supposed to get my hackles up? I assume that there's something ugly and wrong about it that I'm not getting because I'm not educated enough to recognize the insensitivity, and so the different philosophies espoused by the different Dharmas simply seem esoteric to me rather than making me think &quot;oooo boy that's problematic.&quot; I don't need anyone to tell me specifics, or perpetuate the actual ugly stereotype--just get me into the categorical ballpark of which actual groups would stand to feel unjustly drawn upon or appropriated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245791#post1245791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if we wanted to do a new KotE book, we're not going to rely on the same tropes and stereotypes that the original 1998 release did. We'd pretty much want to do a full bottom-to-top rewrite.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ironically, a game which drew so heavily on the tropes and themes of anime would very likely be more popular and timely today than in '98. I know pen and paper games are quite popular in Japan at least--what are the odds that the sort of games that they'd like and enjoy wouldn't track along the same lines as what's popular in their various media? <i>Isekai: The Harem-ing </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 12-07-2019, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T00:14:06-08:00","id":1353270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asimar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1246626#post1246626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just that OPP is scarred that if they do a KOTE20, it will stir some controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have been burned in the (recent) past by fall out from seemingly innocent decisions. And KotE is going to be a difficult property to handle in any situation, or at least difficult to handle without causing a lot of negative push back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T02:13:49-08:00","id":1353288,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it White Wolf, not Onyx Path, that recently got burned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T05:37:14-08:00","id":1353324,"title":"","content":"You know, all I really want from KotE 20th Anniversary Edition is updated rules for their disciplines. Make them standard vampires otherwise, I don't care, I just need a better way to use the disciplines in 20th, because only a couple easily translate, and only a few more than those don't have problematic rules that appear not to have been completely developed and suddenly become OP or open ended or otherwise just kind of stop making sense in the middle of the &quot;systems&quot; section of the description. I can probably home brew all the setting fluff.<br /> <br /> That said, I would love to see Hunter, Mummy, and Demon get their 20th anniversary games. In the case of Hunter and Mummy, I was a fan of both and had as many books as I could find at the time. I never had the opportunity to get Demon, but as I owned at least some part of nearly every other game line, I really wanted to find it, too. I've heard* Demon might need some editing, though, much like what I said above about Kindred of the East.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Yeah, mostly I've heard that here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T16:00:52-08:00","id":1353443,"title":"","content":"KOTE was already niche, with the PUSH to try and get everything behind their 5e version I can't imagine any new 20s coming out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T11:57:47-08:00","id":1353596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353443#post1353443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KOTE was already niche, with the PUSH to try and get everything behind their 5e version I can't imagine any new 20s coming out.</div> </div> </div> </div>With V5 as the flagship for that particular line, I'm really not inclined to trust paradox's decision making on that. I think the WOD5 lines in general are making the same mistake pathfinder is with P2e, in that they're trying to follow D&amp;D's runaway success with simplifying their game mechanics for a wider audience.<br /> <br /> This doesn't exactly work the same for WOD and Pathfinder because they have entirely different audiences. Pathfinder's audience was the people who jumped off at D&amp;D 4e and hate the watered down feel of 5e. WOD's audience is actually rather varied. While the wod writers seem Absolutely Convinced that everyone plays for personal horror And Only personal horror(*cough cough* avatar storm, w20 arcanoi, V5 in general, *cough*), a lot of their playerbase is actually spread on different &quot;layers of play&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some players want to play the neonate struggling with the beast, sure, but other want to play the rise of the new prince, be a dark super hero fighting the forces of corruption, or become great villains in their own right. Best way I can explain it is with VTM as a lens, Some people want to play neonate personal horror, some want to play the ancillae getting things done, some want to play the princes of political and social games, and some want to play the ancient elders pulling the strings towards a personal agenda.<br /> <br /> Classic WOD and it's metaplot allowed all of this, V5(and w20 before that, and Mta Rev before that...) wants everyone to be a neonate.<br /> <br /> Lots of people have problems with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-08-2019, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T12:46:42-08:00","id":1353607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353596#post1353596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With V5 as the flagship for that particular line, I'm really not inclined to trust OPP's decision making on that. I think the WOD5 lines in general are making the same mistake pathfinder is with P2e, in that they're trying to follow D&amp;D's runaway success with simplifying their game mechanics for a wider audience.<br /> <br /> This doesn't exactly work the same for WOD and Pathfinder because they have entirely different audiences. Pathfinder's audience was the people who jumped off at D&amp;D 4e and hate the watered down feel of 5e. WOD's audience is actually rather varied. While the wod writers seem Absolutely Convinced that everyone plays for personal horror And Only personal horror(*cough cough* avatar storm, w20 arcanoi, V5 in general, *cough*), a lot of their playerbase is actually spread on different &quot;layers of play&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some players want to play the neonate struggling with the beast, sure, but other want to play the rise of the new prince, be a dark super hero fighting the forces of corruption, or become great villains in their own right. Best way I can explain it is with VTM as a lens, Some people want to play neonate personal horror, some want to play the ancillae getting things done, some want to play the princes of political and social games, and some want to play the ancient elders pulling the strings towards a personal agenda.<br /> <br /> Classic WOD and it's metaplot allowed all of this, V5(and w20 before that, and Mta Rev before that...) wants everyone to be a neonate.<br /> <br /> Lots of people have problems with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Default play experiences for WoD games tend to get pared down in later editions because it's easier to adjust upward than to take out material. I mean, Masters of the Art was a mass of terrible ideas, but it still got published for the more down-to-earth Revised edition of Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:36:35-08:00","id":1353622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353607#post1353607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Default play experiences for WoD games tend to get pared down in later editions because it's easier to adjust upward than to take out material. I mean, Masters of the Art was a mass of terrible ideas, but it still got published for the more down-to-earth Revised edition of Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I've never seen it be well received.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:49:43-08:00","id":1353626,"title":"","content":"And again: V5 isn't Onyx Path; it's White Wolf, and now Modipheus. That's not just a difference in branding; it's a whole different team of people behind the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:58:28-08:00","id":1353630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353596#post1353596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With V5 as the flagship for that particular line, I'm really not inclined to trust OPP's decision making on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What decision making? Paradox decides what WoD books get made. Onyx Path folks have said they've sent Paradox pitches for 20th books that have been denied. It's not Onyx Path's call.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path doesn't own the WoD. Their only decision making in all of this are what books they're willing to pitch to Paradox. Onyx Path could pitch KotE20 a dozen times, but if Paradox says no, it doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the WOD5 lines in general... </div> </div> </div>Seems kinda weird to generalize when we literally only have one WoD5 line so far to judge on. We need to at least see W5 to see where Paradox is actually headed with these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...are making the same mistake pathfinder is with P2e, in that they're trying to follow D&amp;D's runaway success with simplifying their game mechanics for a wider audience. </div> </div> </div>If they get more people than they lose, is it really a problem?<br /> <br /> I mean, I hate P1e, because it seems to revel in being more complex than D&amp;D 3.X to snatch up their initial target audience of D&amp;D 3.X fans that did not like where D&amp;D 4e went... but there's a point where, &quot;lets be complex for the sake of it,&quot; loses people you don't need to lose. P2e lowering things down to a still pretty complex game, esp. if they want to compete with the runaway success of D&amp;D 5e is kinda necessary. Pathfinder had to do something, or it was going to get left in the dust with dwindling bunch of folks playing their favorite edition being their own customers.<br /> <br /> The situation with WoD5 is pretty different in a number of key ways. The WoD doesn't have a game that lot of fans jumped ship to, people that don't like V5 are just sticking to V20 for the most part, but at the same time most fans that didn't like where V5 went are still pretty cognizant of the Storyteller system needing a major revision that the 20th books weren't intended to do. Whether you want to call it &quot;watered down&quot; or not, the pre-V5 WoD games need a D&amp;D 5e level rebuild that's more accessible if they want to grow the brand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Classic WOD and it's metaplot allowed all of this, V5(and w20 before that, and Mta Rev before that...) wants everyone to be a neonate. </div> </div> </div>Eh... I want to agree with you on this, but you're exaggerating beyond necessity.<br /> <br /> V5 is definitely written to too narrow of an audience. The idea that W20 (either WtA or WtO) or MtA Rev were, or OP in general feels this is how things should be done just doesn't hold water.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:40:27-08:00","id":1353656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353630#post1353630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What decision making? Paradox decides what WoD books get made. Onyx Path folks have said they've sent Paradox pitches for 20th books that have been denied. It's not Onyx Path's call.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path doesn't own the WoD. Their only decision making in all of this are what books they're willing to pitch to Paradox. Onyx Path could pitch KotE20 a dozen times, but if Paradox says no, it doesn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'll change my statement to paradox's decision making and apologize for my ignorance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353630#post1353630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems kinda weird to generalize when we literally only have one WoD5 line so far to judge on. We need to at least see W5 to see where Paradox is actually headed with these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly probably, but VTM has been the flagship that set the standard for a while now. If they're messing up white wolf's baby, that spells trouble. Last time that happened was when the week of nightmares split the community opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353630#post1353630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they get more people than they lose, is it really a problem?<br /> <br /> I mean, I hate P1e, because it seems to revel in being more complex than D&amp;D 3.X to snatch up their initial target audience of D&amp;D 3.X fans that did not like where D&amp;D 4e went... but there's a point where, &quot;lets be complex for the sake of it,&quot; loses people you don't need to lose. P2e lowering things down to a still pretty complex game, esp. if they want to compete with the runaway success of D&amp;D 5e is kinda necessary. Pathfinder had to do something, or it was going to get left in the dust with dwindling bunch of folks playing their favorite edition being their own customers.<br /> <br /> The situation with WoD5 is pretty different in a number of key ways. The WoD doesn't have a game that lot of fans jumped ship to, people that don't like V5 are just sticking to V20 for the most part, but at the same time most fans that didn't like where V5 went are still pretty cognizant of the Storyteller system needing a major revision that the 20th books weren't intended to do. Whether you want to call it &quot;watered down&quot; or not, the pre-V5 WoD games need a D&amp;D 5e level rebuild that's more accessible if they want to grow the brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a person who liked pathfinder, the system wasn't complex for the sake of being complex. It was complex because it capitalized on what turned players off from 4e and 5e, having more options to customize your character rather then reducing them. It's what is turning people off with P2e, the system is complex but it doesn't let you customize. All of the feat chains are very clearly intended to work a certain way and going outside that makes you a less effective character.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the storyteller system is okay. It's slow and drags out complicated encounters like combat, but it's also better a simulating those encounters than D20's &quot;My number is high so I can't fail&quot; system. It could probably use some work, but I don't see V5's changes as better in any regard and change for the sake of change is not a good selling point in my books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353630#post1353630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... I want to agree with you on this, but you're exaggerating beyond necessity.<br /> <br /> V5 is definitely written to too narrow of an audience. The idea that W20 (either WtA or WtO) or MtA Rev were, or OP in general feels this is how things should be done just doesn't hold water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, probably. I may just be paranoid. I Really don't like the trend that w20(solid setting, less than solid crunch) and V5(obvious holes in the setting And mechanics) have set though.<br /> <br /> A one of the most controversial design changes in WOD, releasing time of judgement before revealing and then moving all production to nwod/cod, was proceeded by the writers first deciding the needed to de-power the setting via 6th great maelstrom/avatar storm. I just don't want anything turning out like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-08-2019, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T10:45:31-07:00","id":1395623,"title":"","content":"That I would like to know too. As I whas to young to start with the original WoD I would love to get everything a 20th Anniversary edition because those then will get a german translation via Ulisses Spiele. Some of them would be translated for the first time too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T11:41:25-07:00","id":1395631,"title":"","content":"It looks like Paradox is shutting down the X20 lines; they're letting Onyx Path finish up 