attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:06:53-07:00","id":1395774,"title":"","content":"Eh, the schedule's missing the Technocracy Reloaded stretch goals (which we know are coming), and then there's the question of whether Victorian Mage gets a KS. (And I think Ghost Hunters is 20th, and that's getting a KS.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T07:14:32-07:00","id":1395838,"title":"","content":"4<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353263#post1353263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know pen and paper games are quite popular in Japan at least--what are the odds that the sort of games that they'd like and enjoy wouldn't track along the same lines as what's popular in their various media? <i>Isekai: The Harem-ing </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ahahahaha<br /> <br /> He's got a point though: The Japanese at least don't really care all that much about how you mangle their culture. You should really see how they think europeans work. They expect liberties to be taken. They built up their own mysticism for westerners to misconstrue. Just avoid the Imperial japanese army and you'll be fine. <br /> <br /> We live in the information age, far moreso than what we had in the 90's It's far easier to get accurate information about another country or culture than it was before. The issue is more &quot;White people afraid of looking racist&quot; than an actual issue. It should be pretty easy to update the rules and replace the more egregious errors with common sense solutions. <br /> <br /> I take issue with the fact that WW/OP are happy to butcher european culture with the crude stereotypes of the Lasombra/Tzmisce/Ravnos/Fianna/ShadowLords/GetOfFenrir/AndSoOn/AndSoForth but have the need to keep non whites of everywhere else on a pedastool (after all, europeans invented evil. That Imperial japanese army? Learned from us.) <br /> Either fuck with all of us or fuck with none of us. The world has modernized. Asia and Africa are now places with dense cities. They aren't fantasy traditional dreamlands anymore. <br /> <hr /><br /> I just remembered the elephant that would be in the KOTE room. <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The World of Darkness is not a gameline that should fear censorship. What kind of self respecting satire driven goth-punk setting <b>kowtows</b> to authority? <br /> <br /> Three possible strats: <br /> 1- ALL HAIL THAT COUNTRY, WE'RE COMPLETELY SINCERE. <br /> 2- </span></span></span><b>\u808f\u4f60\u5988 (You may get points for this in other countries)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3- Just avoid talking about the modern mainland. Focus on it's neighbours (That don't begin with T) <br /> <br /> Just not doing east asia might be 'safe' but it really doesn't give you much access to the most populous markets in the world. Even if you can't get a book sold in the that place there are still other very populous rapidly developing economies in Asia to cater to. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_sortable text_table_wikitable text_table_jquery-tablesorter\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">2</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India\" target=\"_blank\">India</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">1,324,009,090</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">3</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indonesia\" target=\"_blank\">Indonesia</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">255,462,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">5</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangladesh\" target=\"_blank\">Bangladesh</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">158,762,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">7</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan\" target=\"_blank\">Japan</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">126,891,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">8</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippines\" target=\"_blank\">Philippines</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">100,699,395</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">9</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam\" target=\"_blank\">Vietnam</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">91,812,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">11</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey\" target=\"_blank\">Turkey</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">78,214,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">12</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thailand\" target=\"_blank\">Thailand</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">69,666,666</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">13</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myanmar\" target=\"_blank\">Myanmar</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">56,480,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">14</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korea\" target=\"_blank\">South Korea</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">50,617,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">18</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malaysia\" target=\"_blank\">Malaysia</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">31,032,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">19</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepal\" target=\"_blank\">Nepal</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">28,038,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">23</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan\" target=\"_blank\">Taiwan</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">23,455,000</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_sortable_tr text_table_wikitable_tr text_table_jquery-tablesorter_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">27</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambodia\" target=\"_blank\">Cambodia</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_sortable_td text_table_wikitable_td text_table_jquery-tablesorter_td\">15,040,000</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Now I don't know much about these nations, but the ones we think of as 'poor' now like Myanmar and Cambodia have phenomenal economic growth rates right now, and'll probably be respectable economies within the next decade. Perhaps you'd not get as great returns with middle-man translators and publishers, but you'll be setting yourself up for much bigger returns when these places start to gain disposable income. Wan Kuei are cool/fun dudes. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And maybe if WoD finds its way into the that country... well, that could be some interesting publicity. If that country really is the issue, I feel like you'd be losing some literary integrity for the World of Darkness to avoid taking a stance. Honesty is the best policy. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T07:18:29-07:00","id":1395839,"title":"","content":"I can't believe my big post got eaten. <br /> <br /> A short version: <br /> <br /> Am I right in assuming that KOTE reluctance has something to do with the PRC? <br /> <br /> Is that really something the gothic punk World of Darkness should be concerned about? <br /> <br /> Other east asian economies are highly populated with fast growing economies and it would be really good to deliver a KOTE product to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T07:24:05-07:00","id":1395840,"title":"","content":"KotE reluctance has nothing to do with PRC. It has to so with the fact that KotE would need a complete rewrite to match today's standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T08:16:44-07:00","id":1395846,"title":"","content":"If you mean you can't copy paste, sure. If you mean the subject matter is &quot;Bad&quot;... <br /> <br /> It mostly isn't. I mean, if you get your understanding of &quot;racism&quot; from a gatekeeping ruling body of predominantly middle class white women, then yeah, it's &quot;bad&quot;. If you aren't into patronizing people, it really needs little more than an edit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T09:34:26-07:00","id":1395853,"title":"","content":"I refer you to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1245791#post1245791\">this post</a> from earlier in this very thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T09:58:12-07:00","id":1395856,"title":"","content":"Yes, he's said that, but I don't think so. I don't think KOTE needs to be changed to that extent. And if we include DAV20... Well, DAV20 has shown us that the 20th line is pretty flexible. Just use better terminology and accept the realities of modern asia. Since this is a 20th line, putting in a lot more super-cool Dharma stuff, rather than giving us a shallow look at things, would do the game line a solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T10:50:30-07:00","id":1396041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1395631#post1395631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like Paradox is shutting down the X20 lines; they're letting Onyx Path finish up the projects they already have in the pipeline, but if it isn't already on the schedule you're probably not going to see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To which my thought is, why?<br /> <br /> V5 released in 2018. W5 isn\u2019t scheduled for release until 2021. At that rate M5 won\u2019t be out until 2024, C5 not until 2027 and Wr5 not until 2030.<br /> <br /> It makes no sense to shutter lines four years before the replacement is available. Shuttering Mage in 2023 for a year of hype to the new edition? Sure. Close it down for nearly half a decade and hope people come back?<br /> <br /> Now, maybe Paradox will get its act together and speed up production; but we\u2019re two year in on V5 and there\u2019s been, what? Core, Anarchs, Camarilla, Fall of Longdon and Chicago by Night actually released with maybe two more books in process ahead of W5?<br /> <br /> All evidence is that Paradox can\u2019t manage more than two books a year and it\u2019s gonna need to keep supporting V5 in addition to follow on books for W5. If anything, M5 in 2024 is probably too ambitious.<br /> <br /> It wouldn\u2019t be the first time someone\u2019s made a bone-headed move in the name of \u201cnot confusing the market,\u201d but that still doesn\u2019t make it a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T12:21:09-07:00","id":1396055,"title":"","content":"While I don't think it defends Paradox's reluctance to not green light 20th books (esp. for lines far from their 5e releases):<br /> <br /> Paradox is doing something a bit different here: having multiple groups developing books. Modiphius, Onyx Path, and now Hunters are all working on books with Paradox operating more as a manager and keep things consistent. The rate of book releases is going to be really different from what we're used to as different companies do things in different ways.<br /> <br /> Paradox could offer M5 to another company to get released in 2022 once they feel like the &quot;formula&quot; of 5e is better setup, and with different teams there isn't as much of a backlog issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T05:33:51-07:00","id":1397274,"title":"","content":"At this point I'm hoping someone much smarter than I starts a fan project to slowly adapt pre-V5 WOD to the Story path system. This and Storyteller's Vault are my great hope for the IP. If V5 is any kind of useful indicator of what's to come, I'm just not interested in the sorts of games Paradox wants people running or playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T09:29:13-07:00","id":1397311,"title":"","content":"The only problem with VTM is the combat and XP effecient character building. <br /> <br /> For the latter problem, you just need to offer Flat XP rates for Attributes/Abilities/Virtues and then give people a discipline array (2/1/0) because discplines work nicely as X-level. <br /> Maybe Composure is a better attribute than Appearance, and I kinda like willpower being a derived stat, though I'd do it between resolve and courage (Or courage+Conviction if you've seen my Conscience+conviction idea) <br /> <br /> For the former, don't roll damage or soak for just take half the dicepool (This obviously doesn't apply to things like fire) and do multiple actions all at once (and decrease the number available) and get rid of the 'declare actions phase and just do stuff. <br /> There's lots of little things to change regarding disciplines and such, but that's the core of the issue. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for V5's metaplot... <br /> <br /> On one hand, A good deal of the metaplot can make sense if you think enough about it. The Camarilla downsizing and then following my economic plan to become the best sect ever would be a good long term strat even if not great in the short term. The Tremere putting up a facade of disunity to avoid looking like a dangerous monopoly that needs to be clipped back is a near perfect plan. The Settites joining the Anarchs to take control of it could work wonders. <br /> <br /> The SI only kinda works if you assume it's just elders directing a neonate cull and the organizations aren't actually that connected. It doesn't work at all if you look at it as-written, it's logistically impossible. <br /> <br /> The Gehenna war only works if it's a <i>lie. </i> Let's say the Sabbat elders saw what the Camarilla was doing and liked it, so they sent their angry neonates off to explode and quietly joined the Cam (On the condition that they can worship openly, which the Cam conceeded) whilst the Elders disapearing is just them avoiding all the cullings and the angry neonates who are responding. The angry sabbat survivors will someday come back with a vengance. <br /> <br /> The Hecatta doesn't work at all. Sure, you can organize the coup, but after than you should just join the Camarilla not... join to become a singular bloodline. <br /> <br /> So like, if you assume I'm right here and maybe we've got some misinformation about the Hecata subsect, it can kinda work well. But now the big problem is that sectarian conflict now just looks like <i>D</i><i>emocrats</i> vs <i>Republicans. </i>The hugely asymetrical nature of what came before still works better. I want to be Oppressed and fight it, that's what I play vampire for. Democrats vs Republicans is not as interesting conflict. <br /> <br /> Like, there's still a chance for V5's storyline to be awesome, but I don't have high hopes because it looks like they'll go a different way (Even moreso democrats VS republicans but somehow vampires are the little guys that fear big goverment.) <br /> <br /> The rules are bad tho. The good things I have to say about the rules are like positive nitpicks rather than something worth talking about. I suppose the very abstract combat system is fast if you're into that. Maybe we can move forward with some of V5's metaplot and more VTM rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T20:03:11-07:00","id":1397882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1397274#post1397274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point I'm hoping someone much smarter than I starts a fan project to slowly adapt pre-V5 WOD to the Story path system. This and Storyteller's Vault are my great hope for the IP. If V5 is any kind of useful indicator of what's to come, I'm just not interested in the sorts of games Paradox wants people running or playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't, since now things are unknown again because of the restructuring and changes that came post-V5 controversies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T11:29:05-07:00","id":1398390,"title":"","content":"Oh, cross-posted this already elsewhere but repeating here:<br /> <br /> With the Wraith: Afterlife game on the horizon, it sounds like a Wraith5e is in the cards with Paradox's playbook.<br /> <br /> And additionally if we take into consideration that Orpheus trademark filed by Paradox a year ago...it sounds like the plan is to have Wraith and Orpheus exist side-by-side in the same edition, and not have the one &quot;ghost gameline&quot;. Which ideally means better integration among each other. Especially since, from what I've gathered, despite Wr20 having Or20 in the same book, there was not a resurgence of Wraith X Orpheus games occurring. <br /> <br /> ...conversely, I'm taking this as soft confirmation that there indeed won't be any more official Wr20 books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T10:52:26-07:00","id":1399100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1398390#post1398390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Wraith: Afterlife game on the horizon, it sounds like a Wraith5e is in the cards with Paradox's playbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the requirement to get an X5 title is having a video game in development, I'd say there's dim hope of seeing M5 any time soon; its magic system relies so much on on player creativity and GM improvisation that I don't see how a computer game would be able to handle Mage and still look remotely like Mage.<br /> <br /> And in the line of WoD development it was Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and then Wraith... so the crickets surrounding anything M5 related while the video game likely associated with a Wr5 is now in development is rather... telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T16:14:46-07:00","id":1399158,"title":"","content":"That seems... lacking support. For all that we like to forget they exist sometimes, Mage got an IF game at the same time as Vampire as the first new products of the new WoD era. That didn't lead to M5 happening before Werewolf got video games.<br /> <br /> Paradox is under no obligation to keep the video game side of things and the TT RPG side of things on the same release order.<br /> <br /> Wraith getting a video game is good evidence for Wr5 being in the works, simply because it shows that Paradox is invested in developing the gameline, not that Wr5 is &quot;next.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T13:36:57-07:00","id":1399362,"title":"","content":"Meh, there\u2019s a difference between IF and something like Bloodlines or the Werewolf and Wraith games look to be.<br /> <br /> They may not have an obligation to keep things synched up, but just the fact that you think Wr5 might be in development because of a Wraith video game (after V5 and Bloodlines 2 in development and W5 and a Werewolf game in development) indicates you do see the causal link (which is likely the benefit of cross-promotion).<br /> <br /> Mage is hard to make into the sort of CRPG video game the others look to be. While there\u2019s even fewer spheres than there are discipline powers, Werewolf gifts or Wraith Arcanoi powers; spheres are both more adaptable and the way paradigm, practice and tools interacts with them lead to such different results that you\u2019d basically need nine different animations for the same rote based on who\u2019s using it.<br /> <br /> You\u2019d probably have to build it with a specific protagonist (instead of the build your own protagonist approach you can do with, say, Bloodlines) with a set paradigm and linear story (so you can better direct the \u201cimprov\u201d nature of Mage spells... basically turn every non-combat magical challenge into a dialogue tree) to not end up with a generic \u201cwizard protagonist\u201d type of feel.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a Technocracy protagonist video game would probably be the easiest... you can then limit the \u201cmagick\u201d to specific devices/props the character is given to solve the current problem and the shared paradigm makes it easier on production time because different Conventions can use the same animations.<br /> <br /> I know lots of people think all this good stuff is just around the corner... but all I\u2019ve seen is a production schedule that can barely handle two book a years and a not quite ready for release video game and twice others in earlier phases of development.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m bracing myself for what\u2019s currently in the OP pipeline for M20 to be the last new material we get for Mage until M40 could be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T20:57:10-07:00","id":1399990,"title":"","content":"Frankly, what has me the most curious is how we have yet to hear about a Changeling video game.<br /> <br /> Like, I like Wraith, but of the canceled gamelines even I'd admit that Changeling was the more approachable gameline. Buy-in as &quot;you play a fae soul in a human body!&quot; is waaay less steep then &quot;sooo...you died.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T16:27:13-07:00","id":1404318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1399990#post1399990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, what has me the most curious is how we have yet to hear about a Changeling video game.<br /> <br /> Like, I like Wraith, but of the canceled gamelines even I'd admit that Changeling was the more approachable gameline. Buy-in as &quot;you play a fae soul in a human body!&quot; is waaay less steep then &quot;sooo...you died.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That won't matter as much on the video game front.<br /> <br /> A lot of video-gamers care more about how responsive combat is and decision trees actually affecting the story than any initial role-play buy-in. Consider the fact that most video-gamers play a large array of different games with from different genres that all push suspension of disbelief in different directions.<br /> <br /> If you a hobbyist video-gamer picked up a game about playing an alien dragon from another dimension, their reaction would be &quot;cool, but is it fun to play?&quot;.Suspension of Disbelief is a much more abundant resource in video game culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T01:28:08-07:00","id":1405032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1353626#post1353626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again: V5 isn't Onyx Path; it's White Wolf, and now Modipheus. That's not just a difference in branding; it's a whole different team of people behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asterisk: With the exception of, of course, some contract writers having worked for all of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T20:35:31-07:00","id":1405239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1404318#post1404318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That won't matter as much on the video game front.<br /> <br /> A lot of video-gamers care more about how responsive combat is and decision trees actually affecting the story than any initial role-play buy-in. Consider the fact that most video-gamers play a large array of different games with from different genres that all push suspension of disbelief in different directions.<br /> <br /> If you a hobbyist video-gamer picked up a game about playing an alien dragon from another dimension, their reaction would be &quot;cool, but is it fun to play?&quot;.Suspension of Disbelief is a much more abundant resource in video game culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>...no.<br /> <br /> They care just as much if the setting, plot, and characters displayed is cool enough to want to play them. Especially since gameplay is hard to convey in a trailer when you can't figure out how gameplay feels...until you actually by and play it.<br /> <br /> You can't put gameplay on the back of the box or in a trailer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T00:19:00-07:00","id":1405255,"title":"","content":"&quot;So... you died&quot; has significantly more mass-appeal than &quot;you play a kid with a fae soul&quot; <br /> <br /> I mean, the latter is far more artsy and maybe you'd get some big word-of-mouth appeal from surprising players with a good, very dark story; but if you don't have that good, very dark story, wouldn't it be better to play it safe with wraith from a business perspective? And Changeling is a setting where you, from all outside perspectives a kid, stab up other &quot;kids&quot; in subway stations; Controversy might make sales but it also gets you banned in a lot of places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:05:05-07:00","id":1405271,"title":"","content":"I'm going to agree with MyWifeIsScary. Changeling's premise is a lot less immediately approachable than &quot;you play as a ghost&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell, the existence of games like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murdered:_Soul_Suspect\" target=\"_blank\">Murdered: Soul Suspect</a> is proof that &quot;ghost simulator&quot; is already a viable sub-genre. Heck, we knew that as far back as (the ironically named) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geist_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> on the Gamecube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:04:59-07:00","id":1405411,"title":"","content":"Why people always think changeling PCs should be kids? I seriously never got the impressions that this was the intended/classic way to play it reading the books.<br /> <br /> <br /> Buy Anyway. I agree that wraith is much easier to sell.<br /> <br /> I think a changeling game would be better explored in a episodic game, like life is strange, telltale games, etc. Changeling should totally be story game, not a action game.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:17:30-07:00","id":1405415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1405411#post1405411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why people always think changeling PCs should be kids? I seriously never got the impressions that this was the intended/classic way to play it reading the books.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not all of them, of course; but the Seemings mirror age groups: <u>Child</u>lings, Wilders, and Grumps, mirroring children, teenagers, and adults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T02:04:16-07:00","id":1405523,"title":"","content":"Pre-C20, Seemings were explicitly tied to age (though living in a Freehold can slow aging); which definitely has had a lasting impact on the perception of the game<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that CtD 2e put it this way: &quot;childling (mortal birth through approximately age 12), wilder (13-25) and grump (26 and older).&quot; CtD was setup such that 26 is old, where for most people that's when you're just starting truly independent adulthood.<br /> <br /> C20 did a decent job of fixing this by decoupling Seeming from age, but as Dataweaver noted, there's still a psychological aspect to it where a 20 year old childling is expected to be immature in a fashion most people are going to see as notably so for their age. Even grumps, the mature Seeming, haven't completely lost themselves to Banality despite their acceptance that it's a losing battle; most grumps are going to appear to be &quot;eccentric&quot; and defy social norms by remaining committed to activities society associates with childhood and not moving on to having &quot;normal&quot; adult lives. It's nearly impossible for CtD to get away from the idea that the characters value childhood and immaturity that gives the impression that the game is about playing kids.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T02:07:04-07:00","id":1405525,"title":"","content":"The game goes on to say that the latter category have usually sucumbed to banality (Though I suppose they're a much larger bracket...) which makes me think you're supposed to play young. Also from my experience of the few players who wanted to play changeling instead of the usual vampire or werewolf... being a kid is a lot of the appeal to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T18:29:55-07:00","id":1405718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1405255#post1405255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And Changeling is a setting where you, from all outside perspectives a kid, stab up other &quot;kids&quot; in subway stations; Controversy might make sales but it also gets you banned in a lot of places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...what?<br /> <br /> Whose Changeling games have you been playing in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T08:04:50-07:00","id":1405944,"title":"","content":"Sigh so now is Storyteller's Vault the last torch held up for the old school World of Darkness Content?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:08:52-07:00","id":1406018,"title":"","content":"Well, there's still a few books in the pipeline from Onyx Path for 20th era games, but it does seem like after those are done, that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:28:02-07:00","id":1406021,"title":"","content":"Yeah. At this point, the best we can hope for is that whoever does the rest of the 5th edition books does a better job than was done with V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T00:05:21-07:00","id":1406391,"title":"","content":"If people can match the design qualities and innovation of V5, without getting bogged down by edition war baggage, across all the original lines, then that would be outstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T09:34:38-07:00","id":1406453,"title":"","content":"So ya take V2*<br /> and then ya take V20<br /> and then you mash them together taking the best of both (with a few people who have diverse opinions because some things V1/2 did is subtly really clever but got lost in revised translation)<br /> and then you try hard to streamline the thing and work on things people don't like in a way that captures the intentions of what came before as well as broad appeal, but you also need to understand that broad appeal doesn't mean 'accessible' when it comes to fluff.<br /> and then you give the V5 metaplot some consideration because some of it's actually pretty good and some of my &quot;conspiracy theories&quot; [read: The most logical solution to a clear problem] are actually pretty good.<br /> and then you remember to edit the book.<br /> <br /> and then you have the perfect, risk free x6 game which makes the overwhelming majority of people happy. I'd buy shares. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*V2 is like V1 but better right? Honestly, haven't read much of it. Bit of a blind spot for me. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T12:15:39-07:00","id":1406484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1406453#post1406453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So ya take V2*<br /> and then ya take V20<br /> and then you mash them together taking the best of both (with a few people who have diverse opinions because some things V1/2 did is subtly really clever but got lost in revised translation)<br /> and then you try hard to streamline the thing and work on things people don't like in a way that captures the intentions of what came before as well as broad appeal, but you also need to understand that broad appeal doesn't mean 'accessible' when it comes to fluff.<br /> and then you give the V5 metaplot some consideration because some of it's actually pretty good and some of my &quot;conspiracy theories&quot; [read: The most logical solution to a clear problem] are actually pretty good.<br /> and then you remember to edit the book.<br /> <br /> and then you have the perfect, risk free x6 game which makes the overwhelming majority of people happy. I'd buy shares.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*V2 is like V1 but better right? Honestly, haven't read much of it. Bit of a blind spot for me. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>You are no authority on what makes any WoD game good or not. Your account of any of the games\u2019 development has an equivalent value to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T13:44:48-07:00","id":1406503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1406484#post1406484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are no authority on what makes any WoD game good or not. Your account of any of the games\u2019 development has an equivalent value to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Everyone is entitled to their opinion.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T17:38:49-07:00","id":1406531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1405239#post1405239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...no.<br /> <br /> They care just as much if the setting, plot, and characters displayed is cool enough to want to play them. Especially since gameplay is hard to convey in a trailer when you can't figure out how gameplay feels...until you actually by and play it.<br /> <br /> You can't put gameplay on the back of the box or in a trailer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but my point was that suspension of disbelief wasn't going to be the sticking point on a changeling game.<br /> <br /> I'm also of the opinion that being a fae hiding among humans to try and restore wonder to the world is a cool enough concept to attract gamers as long as it's handled well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T21:27:25-07:00","id":1408098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1405944#post1405944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh so now is Storyteller's Vault the last torch held up for the old school World of Darkness Content?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correct. Hell even Developers for lines are using Storytellers Vault along with the majority of Freelancers to keep giving us books that were blocked by Paradox. Theres awesome stuff on there for CtD, MtA, WtA and WtO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T04:08:42-07:00","id":1408123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1245762-so-what-s-next?p=1408098#post1408098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Correct. Hell even Developers for lines are using Storytellers Vault along with the majority of Freelancers to keep giving us books that were blocked by Paradox. Theres awesome stuff on there for CtD, MtA, WtA and WtO.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the worst is, it seems Paradox is even blocking further translations of M20. That or I will get a hell of an expensive Crowdfunding if they just want to allow it Ulisses Spiele when all the books are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","v